or had expired. 
They were probably all set around the same time.
Once they had been reset remote shell started again.

As a point of interest when the same problem occurs on  HP-UX you get the
message that the password has expired but
on DU 4.0 you only get 'permission denied'  which sounds like a different
problem and, according to the man pages, should
only occur when failing .rhosts verification.

Thanks to those who replied with checking permissions suggestions. I am
including a reply which actually suggests there
may be a problem with a fix.



>From Toni Harbaugh-Blackford

Are you using the password expiration warning on the 3 alphas
which are reporting the problem?

There is a bug in 4.0D (possible other versions) where rsh'ing into a DU box
running
enhanced security will fail if the password of the account will expire within
the
'd_pw_expire_warning' interval.  Compaq has a provisional patch, but the patch
is not
part of any public patchkit yet.

