Reply from Laurent Sainte-Marthe 
--------------------------------
Hello,

I had a similar problem not with the filemanager, but with dtmail.
In fact, problem came from the file /var/tmp/sdtdbcache_* which depends
on the display and must be owned by the session user.
If this file doesn't exist or isn't owned by the session user, printing failed. 

After removing the wrong sdtdbcache_* file if it exists, you can create 
the right file with the command :

 /usr/dt/bin/sdtdbcache -init
 
In my case, I had to modify /usr/dt/config/Xstartup and 
/usr/dt/config/Xreset to correctly manage sdtdbcache files

I hope this can helps you

 Laurent
 
