From tru64-unix-managers  Mon May 08 10:51:30 2000
From: "Galama, Dagmar" <Dagmar.Galama () nl ! origin-it ! com>
Date: Mon, 08 May 2000 10:51:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: ADDITIONAL SUMMARY: Two questions about btcreate (Bootable tape)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079346819469

I received some extra information about the btcreate-utility from Shivraja
Gowda. Interesting too, I think...

"First question:

The problem reported here [problem with two or more filesets per AdvFS 
domain] has been fixed in our latest version V5.0 and above. And a problem 
request has been sent to fix this in V4.0D and above.

Second question:

Without -d option we cannot run the btcreate utility in non-interactive
mode.
Actually this turns out to be a problem in the manpage of btcreate since
this is not mentioned.  The solution to your problem is to use the -d option

with other options as below:

/usr/sys/bin/btcreate -f -k MACHINENAME -m mfs/disk_partition -d
/usr/sys/bin -t nrmt0h -a usr/lib/sabt/etc/addlist -s
/usr/lib/sabt/etc/fslist

The V4.0f btcreate manpage describes the -d option and a request has been
sent 
to update the man page for btcreate with this information."

Cheers,

Dagmar

