From tru64-unix-managers  Wed May 03 20:21:40 2000
From: Frank Wortner <frank () bondnet ! com>
Date: Wed, 03 May 2000 20:21:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:  NFS Hangs Between Tru64 Unix 5.0 and Network Appliance
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079346819398

Thanks to Lee Hank, Paul A. Sand,  and Richard Bond for their replies.

Their suggestions included:

1) Upgrade the Network Appliance Filer's OS to a later version.  We have
5.2.2,  and NetApp's latest is 5.3.5R2.

2) Upgrade Tru64 Unix from 5.0 to the recently shipped 5.0A.

3) Check that NetApp supports NFS V3.  (It does.  All the NFS stats show
only NFS V3 activity and no NFS V2 activity.)

4) Check for other network or NFS errors.  (Unfortunately,  there are none
indicated on either Tru64 or NetApp.)

I'll probably do 1 and 2 (in that order) when we can spare the downtime.

Thanks again!

Frank

